{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-93705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-93705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-93705" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c01b3d0291242c3722660b979fd1ef3feac8b402b4cc5cd324c3320d678056db"} {"question" "q-93705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-93705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "-{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-93705" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ into the expression for $Q(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =61.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c01b3d0291242c3722660b979fd1ef3feac8b402b4cc5cd324c3320d678056db"} {"question" "q-94090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-7"] ["math" "16"] ["math" "34"] ["math" "61"] ["math" "65"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "61"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{3}(2{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{x}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c01b3d0291242c3722660b979fd1ef3feac8b402b4cc5cd324c3320d678056db"} {"question" "q-94099" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94099" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94099" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ b & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=-2{x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2){x}_{1}^{2}+(-5){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-5){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-3){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-10{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{-10}{2}=-5\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -5 \\\\ -5 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2$ and $b=-5.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=-2+(-5)=-7.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94116" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "c01b3d0291242c3722660b979fd1ef3feac8b402b4cc5cd324c3320d678056db"} {"question" "q-94116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-5"] ["math" "-7"] ["math" "2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-94116" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-7"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-140929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the quadratic form \n$Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ \nEvaluate $Q(x)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca7f4f882bcaf6e54b0"} {"question" "q-140929" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We are given that \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression for $Q(x)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-4\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =9+12+0+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14073138/state.json" "file_sha256" "0f5eef475e6468f4fb8265e85d1e38223d98ecb571802ca